      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change will allow to start Bluetooth no only when the persisted state is `BLUETOOTH_ON_BLUETOOTH` but when it is `BLUETOOTH_ON_AIRPLANE` too.\n\nI hate these variables name as they are not very explicit, but `BLUETOOTH_ON_AIRPLANE` indicate that \"Bluetooth is off\" because \"airplane mode is on\", but \"Bluetooth was on\" before. It help to keep track that Bluetooth will need to restart, once airplane mode ends.\n\n----\n\nIn this method we are already in BLE_ON mode, so according to your repro step, we got here in the first place because Airplane Mode was disabled, and we are more likely to be turning Bluetooth ON.\nIn a normal case, the persisted state would be `ON_BLUETOOTH` and we would start.\nBut in this case of stress testing with race condition, I believe the state is at `ON_AIRPLANE` because airplane mode is activated again. Therefor we don\u0027t want to start.\n\n---\n\nThe only explanation I can see is if the airplane mode has been toggled twice before the first MESSAGE_ENABLE was handled. And while the first `sendEnableMsg` from `handleAirplaneModeChanged` is in the queue, we call `handleAirplaneModeChanged` a second time, goes into `forceToOffFromModeChange`, but has nothing to do yet and doesn\u0027t un-enqueue the message.\n\n---\n\nPlease, can you open a bug and upload associated bugreport ? (you can assign it to me). Because of above comment, I don\u0027t think this CL is the fix we want.\nLet me know if I misunderstood anything",
